  "components": [
    {
      "id": "maestro",
      "name": "Maestro (WCB ;M verbs)",
      "kind": "wcb-verb",
      "confidence": "high",
      "firmware": "WCB 6.2.1_021242RSEP2026",
      "routing": {
        "class": "wcb-verb",
        "notes": "Run Sequence (;M<id><seq>) works on every WCB firmware. The comma forms, named \"(WCB 6.2+)\", need WCB 6.2.1 on the board that parses them: WCB 6.1.x reads any comma form as ;M<id>0 and runs subroutine 0 instead (6.1.5 WCB.ino:4871-4876). A 6.2.1 board passes a plain ;M<id>,<n> on to another board as ;M<id><n>, but verbs and subroutines with a parameter travel as typed, so the WCB hosting the Maestro needs 6.2.1 as well (WCB_Maestro.cpp maestroVerbForwardText). Id 0 = every Maestro on the mesh; 1-8 = the Maestro configured with that id (?MAESTRO,M<id>:W<wcb>S<port>:<baud>); 9 = every Maestro configured on the receiving WCB, or its S1 Maestro addressed as the WCB's own number when none is configured (also on 6.1.5, unless that board has a Maestro configured as id 9). Subroutines are Pololu data bytes 0-127: the firmware help says 0-255, but a Pololu data byte cannot exceed 127. Channels are 0-based, 0-23 (Mini Maestro 24). Target is in quarter-microseconds (6000 = 1.5 ms; 0 stops the pulses); speed 0 and acceleration 0 mean unlimited. get* queries take ids 1-8 only and are asynchronous: the answer lands in the RAM variables m<id>pos<ch>, m<id>moving (0/1) and m<id>err (not saved to NVS), which an IF in a separate, later trigger reads (e.g. IF,m2moving=0). Never wrap a get in ;W: the answer would stay on the target board (WCB_Help.cpp:451-459). getMovingState works on Mini Maestro only (Pololu Maestro guide 5.e)."
      },
      "commands": [
        {
          "id": "maestro.trigger",
          "name": "Run Sequence",
          "safety": "movement",
          "encoder": "template",
          "template": ";M{id}{seq}",
          "params": [
            {
              "name": "id",
              "enum": "maestro.id",
              "required": true
            },
            {
              "name": "seq",
              "type": "int",
              "min": 0,
              "max": 127,
              "required": true
            }
          ],
          "examples": [
            ";M11"
          ],
          "commentLabel": "Maestro seq",
          "category": "Sequences"
        },
        {
